// Rule set for the documents the package ships (`assets/**`).
//
// These are instructions an agent reads, not prose a person scans in a column,
// and five rules read them as the wrong kind of document:
//
//   MD013  line length — reflowing an instruction moves where its meaning breaks
//   MD033  inline HTML — the skill bodies and templates use it deliberately
//   MD038  spaces in code spans — a quoted output prefix such as `[warn] `
//          carries its trailing space as part of what is quoted
//   MD028  blank line in blockquote — stacked callouts are the house style here
//   MD029  ordered list prefix — numbers that other documents cite ("steps 3, 4
//          and 5 below") survive a list the prose interrupts
//
// MD024 is configured rather than disabled: a template repeats `Entry 1` under
// each distinct category heading, which is correct under every parent.
//
// MD041 allows a preamble. The seeded `AGENTS.md`
// and `CLAUDE.md` open with the one directive an agent must read first, above
// their top-level heading. The first heading must still be level 1.
{
  "config": {
    "default": true,
    "MD013": false,
    "MD024": { "siblings_only": true },
    "MD028": false,
    "MD029": false,
    "MD033": false,
    "MD038": false,
    "MD041": { "allow_preamble": true },
  },
}
